  "title": "{{PROJECT_NAME}} - ZLens Workbench",
  "metadata": {
    "title": "{{PROJECT_NAME}} - ZLens Workbench",
    "description": "ZLens starter workbench for building domain-first analytics."
  },
  "cells": [
    {
      "id": "intro",
      "type": "markdown",
      "title": "Welcome",
      "source": "# {{PROJECT_NAME}}\n\nZLens is governed analytics written in DQL (**Domain Query Language**), its query language. Together they turn SQL, business terms, notebooks, dashboards, apps, and lineage into one trusted analytics project.\n\n**Core path:** source data -> DQL block -> business_view -> dashboard/app/AI answer.\n\nUse this notebook as your workbench: explore data, promote repeated SQL into reusable blocks, define business vocabulary, and compile the project manifest for lineage and AI-ready context."
    },
    {
      "id": "starter_query",
      "type": "sql",
      "title": "Starter Query",
      "source": "-- Connect a warehouse or add a local DuckDB/file connection, then query your source tables here\n-- Example: SELECT * FROM analytics.customers LIMIT 10;\nselect 1 as customer_count"
    },
    {
      "id": "save_a_query",
      "type": "markdown",
      "title": "Save a query",
      "source": "## Save a query\n\nWhen a query answers a question people ask again, choose **Save as block** on its cell. ZLens saves it as a DQL block in `domains/`, and it appears in Apps under **Data** once it is certified:\n\n```dql\nblock \"Revenue by month\" {\n  domain = \"sales\"\n  owner = \"you@example.com\"\n  query = \"\"\"\n    SELECT date_trunc('month', ordered_at) AS month, SUM(order_total) AS revenue\n    FROM orders\n    GROUP BY 1\n  \"\"\"\n}\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "next_steps",
      "type": "markdown",
      "title": "Next Steps",
      "source": "## Next steps\n\n1. Connect a warehouse or add a local DuckDB/file connection.\n2. Create a business domain with `zlens new domain <name>`.\n3. Save repeated SQL as DQL blocks under `domains/<domain>/blocks/`.\n4. Add shared vocabulary under `domains/<domain>/terms/` and agent guidance under `skills/`.\n5. Run `zlens compile .` and open Lineage to inspect technical and business paths."
    }
  ]
}
